-- Q516: Fix #6
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Wrong (B): Under IRC Section 168(d)(1), the half-year convention treats all property as placed in service at the midpoint of the tax year regardless of actual acquisition date. For 7-year MACRS property using 200% declining balance, the full-year rate is 28.57% (2/7), but the convention halves it to 14.29% in year one. Both Petrov and Santiago receive the identical 14.29% first-year rate.
Wrong (A): The half-year convention is not month-sensitive; both taxpayers receive identical first-year rates regardless of when the property was acquired.
Correct (C): The half-year convention does reduce the first-year rate by half; it does not affect only the final recovery year.
Wrong (D): The half-year convention does not pro-rate by quarter; that describes the mid-quarter convention under Section 168(d)(3), which applies only when more than 40% of property is placed in service in the fourth quarter.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 516;

-- Q531: Fix #6
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Wrong (A): Under Section 453, the installment method calculates a gross profit percentage (total gain divided by contract price) applied to each payment received. Harper''s percentage is 40% ($80,000 gain / $200,000 price) and Mercer''s is 20% ($40,000 gain / $200,000 price). Harper recognizes $20,000 gain on the $50,000 down payment (40%), while Mercer recognizes $10,000 (20%). The method matches gain recognition with cash receipt.
Wrong (B): The percentage depends on each seller''s gain relative to the contract price, so different bases produce different percentages — not a uniform 40%.
Wrong (C): The formula is gain divided by price, not basis divided by price; 60% and 80% reverse the calculation.
Correct (D): The installment method applies regardless of whether a down payment is received; it is the default method for qualifying deferred-payment sales under Section 453.$EXPL$
