-- Q2464: Fix #6
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Wrong (D): Under UCC Section 2-205, a firm offer by a merchant made in a signed writing that assures the offer will be held open is irrevocable for the stated period (up to 3 months) without consideration. This is an exception to the common law rule requiring consideration for option contracts.
Correct (A): A deposit is not required. UCC Section 2-205 specifically eliminates the consideration requirement for a merchant''s firm offer in a signed writing.
Wrong (B): While the common law requires consideration to keep an offer open, UCC Section 2-205 creates an exception for merchants'' signed written offers.
Wrong (C): There is no automatic 5-business-day revocation rule. The offer remains open for the stated period, up to a maximum of 3 months.$EXPL$
