-- Q2473: Fix #6
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Wrong (D): Under the Restatement (Second) of Contracts Section 376, rescission cancels the contract and requires mutual restitution, restoring both parties to their pre-contract positions. This equitable remedy is available for fraud, material misrepresentation, mutual mistake, duress, or failure of consideration.
Correct (A): Rescission does not require a finding of criminal fraud. Civil misrepresentation, as in Stratton''s case, is sufficient to support rescission.
Wrong (B): Rescission restores parties to pre-contract positions through restitution — it does not award double the contract value or punitive multiples.
Wrong (C): Rescission is available for contracts involving any subject matter, not only real property. It applies wherever grounds like fraud or misrepresentation exist.$EXPL$
