-- Q2506: Fix #6
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Wrong (D): Under IRC Sec. 1, a sole proprietorship is not a separate taxable entity. All business income and expenses are reported on Schedule C of Form 1040 as part of the owner''s individual return. Helen''s $68,000 revenue and $22,000 expenses flow through Schedule C.
Correct (A): Schedule E reports rental, royalty, partnership, and S corporation income. Sole proprietor business income belongs on Schedule C, not Schedule E.
Wrong (B): Form 1120 is the corporate income tax return filed by C corporations under IRC Sec. 11. A sole proprietorship is not a corporation and does not file Form 1120.
Wrong (C): Form 1065 is the partnership information return filed under IRC Sec. 701. A sole proprietorship is not a partnership and has no separate entity-level filing requirement.$EXPL$
