  explanation = $EXPL$Wrong (A): Under ASC 815-20-25-75, basis risk occurs when the hedging instrument and the hedged exposure do not move in perfect correlation. Cross-hedging jet fuel with crude oil futures introduces basis risk, as shown by the 7-percentage-point spread between crude oil''s 12% decline and jet fuel''s 5% decline.
