-- Q15832: Fix #9
UPDATE questions SET
  stem = $EXPL$During the audit of Linden Healthcare Group, the engagement team discovers that management omitted a required disclosure about the entity's accounting policy for revenue recognition No dollar amounts are misstated in the financial statements, and all recorded revenue figures are correct. The auditor should evaluate this omission as:$EXPL$,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): AU-C 450.A4. Misstatements include omissions of required disclosures, which can be material even when no quantitative error exists. Users rely on disclosure of accounting policies to interpret the financial statements.
Wrong (A): Materiality encompasses both quantitative amounts and qualitative aspects, including disclosure completeness.
Wrong (B): An omitted disclosure is a misstatement to be evaluated, not a scope limitation that prevents the auditor from performing procedures.
Wrong (D): While the omission may also indicate a control deficiency, its primary significance is its potential effect on the audit opinion, not merely a communication matter. (See ASC 606..)$EXPL$
WHERE id = 15832;

